<Slide style={{
    width: 1280,
    height: 720,
    background: '#FFFFFF',
    padding: '60px 60px',
    flexDirection: 'column',
    fontFamily: '"Arial", "Microsoft YaHei", sans-serif',
}}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#3D7BD9', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 1.6 }}>
        STEP 4 / 7 · HOW WE JUDGE (1/2)
    </Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 34, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#0E3F8C', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 10 }}>
        Scoring: log loss, and a margin of 0.02 nats
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ height: 1, background: '#D6DCE5', marginTop: 12 }} />

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 32, marginTop: 12 }}>
        <Box style={{ width: 564, padding: '10px 16px', background: '#F7F9FC', border: '1px solid #D6DCE5', borderRadius: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#3D7BD9', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 1.2 }}>THE SCORE</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.5, marginTop: 4 }}>
                Three probabilities summing to one. After the match you are charged −log p for what actually
                happened, so a confident miss is expensive. Averaged over matches, in nats — lower is better.
                We never report accuracy: it rewards conviction, not honesty.
            </Text>
        </Box>
        <Box style={{ width: 564, padding: '10px 16px', background: '#F7F9FC', border: '1px solid #D6DCE5', borderRadius: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#3D7BD9', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 1.2 }}>THE MARGIN</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.5, marginTop: 4 }}>
                0.02 nats, read two ways. On one match: pricing a one-in-three event at 32.6% instead of 33.3%.
                On 48 blocks: the finest tick the data can show — nothing smaller is resolvable, whatever we
                claim. Not a low bar, a resolution limit.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', justifyContent: 'center', alignItems: 'center' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#7C8899', letterSpacing: 0.3, marginBottom: 6 }}>
            Two comparisons we already have — this is the ruler's first use, not a finding
        </Text>
        <Image src="assets/fig04.png" style={{ width: 1020, height: 276 }} />
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ padding: '11px 20px', background: '#F0F5FC', borderRadius: 6 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>
            Read the same way: C1 costs 0.0055 nats with an interval that excludes zero; C2 buys back 0.0015
            with one that crosses zero. Both sit inside the margin — separable, and not worth a decision.
        </Text>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', alignItems: 'center', marginTop: 9 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8B97A8' }}>DSC5001 · Statistical Machine Learning I</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#1E4FA8', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>Team 32 · 4/10</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
